functions.sh: replace `mdev -d` with the busybox-compatible setup

Mainline busybox `mdev` has no daemon mode — the `-d` flag is a
postmarketOS-specific patch on top of busybox. With the upstream busybox
that this Nerves system ships, `setup_mdev` fails immediately:

    mdev: invalid option -- 'd'

The upstream busybox approach is to register `mdev` as the kernel's
hotplug helper via `/proc/sys/kernel/hotplug` and do an initial coldplug
pass with `mdev -s`. Each later uevent then forks an `mdev` invocation,
so there is no long-lived daemon to kill — the existing `kill mdev` in
`init` becomes a silent no-op (it already redirects stderr to /dev/null
and `mdev` is not a PID anyway).

--- a/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/functions.sh
+++ b/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/functions.sh
@@ -54,8 +54,11 @@
 }

 setup_mdev() {
-    # Start mdev daemon
-    mdev -d
+    # Mainline busybox mdev has no daemon mode (postmarketOS adds -d via
+    # patches). Use the upstream busybox approach: register mdev as the
+    # kernel's hotplug helper and do an initial coldplug pass.
+    echo /sbin/mdev > /proc/sys/kernel/hotplug
+    mdev -s
 }

 load_modules() {
